# OVERLAY, applied AFTER holybro_sitl.parm — ArduPilot SITL takes `defaults` as
# an ordered comma-separated list and the last file to name a parameter wins.
# Nothing is duplicated here: only what this variant changes.
#
# THE BENCHMARK VARIANT "speed". What it is testing, and what it deliberately
# does NOT touch.
#
# MEASURED 2026-09-14 over a full run: horizontal speed peaked at 0.43 m/s
# against the 0.6 cap, and TRAVEL was 255 s of a 526 s mission — 48.5%, the
# single biggest line in the budget. Half the mission is getting somewhere.
#
# WP_ACC IS NOT RAISED, and that is the whole point of the experiment. The
# base file's own reasoning separates the two: acceleration is what the
# airframe FEELS when a new setpoint appears, and BiguaSim's 0.3-0.5 s
# actuation lag is what turns a sharp demand into an oscillation. Cruise speed
# is only how long it spends at that speed. So this raises the ceiling and
# leaves the demand exactly as gentle as it was.
#
# The other justification in the base file — "a bad position estimate produces
# a slow wander rather than a dash into a wall" — is real and is what this
# benchmark is measuring the cost of. If VO drift or valid landings get worse,
# that is the answer and this overlay loses.
WP_SPD          1.0
# Yaw slew, deg/s. The base file argues FOR 25 in its own comment ("makes it
# ~1.8 s" for a 45 deg turn) and then sets 15. A 90 deg turn costs 6.0 s at 15
# and 3.6 s at 25. The risk it names is smearing the visual odometry through
# the step, which the seed sweep measures directly.
ATC_RATE_WPY_MAX 25
